    "q-37854": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37854",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\,dy\\,dx=$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}x[{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}x{[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡y}{2}]}_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}x(\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡{e}^{x}}{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}x(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}x(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2})\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(-2)^{4}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}-2+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2-1-8+16}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
