    "q-37862": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37862",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,dA,\\,$ where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{x}\\le y\\le \\frac{3}{x}\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over the type I region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{x}\\le y\\le \\frac{3}{x}\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/x}^{3/x}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/x}^{3/x}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1/x}^{3/x}\\frac{2}{1+(2xy)^{2}}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy)]}_{1/x}^{3/x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2))\\,dx \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,dx & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2))[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2))\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2))\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
